  "2026-10-18T21:21:42.236Z",codex-agent,"macOS aggregate now proves 100% workspace regions and 100% lines/functions/branches overall; only one list region remains. Failure diagnostics identify gaps in exact-ID error propagation, late producer-limit validation, and dependency-parent traversal in a library build. Add concrete SDK/CLI cases for a corrupt selected ID, invalid limit with offset, and dependency-only parent selection. Keep native source, binaries, timing receipts and all thresholds unchanged."
  "2026-10-18T21:27:17.010Z",codex-agent,"List-region cases verified: cargo test --locked --test read_contract sdk_ passed 3 tests, including a dependency-only parent through the brief projection, corrupt exact-ID list through SDK and CLI, and bad limit plus offset through SDK and CLI. Focused instrumented run passed 252 library plus 16 read-contract tests; late producer-limit error counts are positive in both library builds, and exact-ID error arms are exercised. Five linked commands passed again (18 executions); pedantic Clippy passed. Native source/binary, benchmark data and thresholds are unchanged. Releasing ownership for the complete three-OS rerun; keep item in progress and PR open, publishing disabled."
  "2026-10-18T23:24:21.137Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1: verified PR thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6tvSRQ against head 48ce0cd. Full-corpus collect_toon_entries currently swallows every symlink_metadata error and can report an incomplete corpus as success. Will retain the vanished-entry NotFound race behavior, propagate all other metadata errors with their original item path, and add a real filesystem regression plus behavior-only revert proof. Existing benchmark receipts remain intact; Linux release-check and three-platform CI will validate the review patch."
  "2026-10-18T23:25:26.416Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the review fix: collect_toon_entries skips only NotFound, propagating every other metadata failure as PmRustError::Io with the listed item path and original source. The regression takes a real tracker directory snapshot, replaces its ancestor with a self-referential directory symlink, and asserts the non-NotFound metadata refusal rather than an empty successful corpus. The existing removed-entry test still checks the allowed NotFound race. No query projection, oracle suite, latency threshold or item-open budget changed."
  "2026-10-18T23:26:32.904Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 behavior-only revert proof: restored only src/workspace.rs to head 48ce0cd, leaving the new filesystem regression unchanged, then ran cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib workspace::tests::directory_snapshots. Exit 101: 1 passed, 1 failed; directory_snapshots_propagate_item_metadata_errors failed with listed item metadata failure was silently skipped, while the vanished-entry regression passed. The metadata error-handling fix has been restored for the clean verification run. The performance lookup and context implementations were not reverted in this review round."
