  "2026-10-19T00:12:39.167Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 Linux release-check progress: formatting, pedantic Clippy and private-item rustdoc passed. The ordinary run has completed 406 tests across 16 suites with zero failures or ignored tests, including all 27 lifecycle differential cases, close, conformance, list, mutation, identity and all 18 orientation cases. The mixed-status pagination walk is still active on the shared host; the instrumented coverage pass, audit and final changelog check remain pending. No gate, fixture or threshold has been weakened."
  "2026-10-19T00:19:57.558Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 Linux release-check milestone: all 482 ordinary tests passed across 20 suites, with zero failed or ignored tests and the published oracle required. This includes the new real-filesystem metadata regression, all unchanged byte-differential suites, identity, release-workflow checks and both item-open regressions. Formatting, pedantic Clippy and private-item rustdoc also passed. The aggregate has started its required branch-instrumented all-target test run; four-dimension coverage, audit and final changelog verification are still pending."
  "2026-10-19T01:05:49.242Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 Linux local just release-check PASSED with isolated home and global Git configuration: formatting, pedantic Clippy, private-item rustdoc, identity audit, required-oracle ordinary and instrumented tests, cargo audit and changelog verification. Exact counts: 482 ordinary + 482 instrumented = 964 passed across 40 suite executions; zero failed or ignored. Coverage is 12005/12005 lines, 1211/1211 functions, 19693/19693 regions and 2926/2926 branches, all 100 percent. Audit retains only the existing allowed RUSTSEC-2024-0449 advisory. All six linked commands also passed (21 executions). The new metadata regression fails with only the fix reverted and passes restored; original get/context revert proofs remain valid. Will push the paired code and append-only tracker changes, then poll exact-head three-platform CI every 60 seconds for up to 40 minutes. No thread reply, resolution, bot mention, merge or publishing action is authorized or planned. Final CI receipts will be linked in PR 94."
  "2026-10-19T14:13:44.407Z",codex-agent,"Related validation evidence from native-context PR #98 at 921275d: the unchanged 3000-item Windows cold-process latency job passed get p95 25.97 ms below 50 ms and context p95 243.88 ms below 250 ms, but list p95 156.14 ms exceeded its unchanged 150 ms ceiling (30 fresh processes). Linux and macOS latency jobs passed. No list implementation or latency gate was changed in that context commit. Retaining this observation on the existing performance item rather than creating a duplicate; a subsequent exact-head run remains pending. Job receipt: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39264985747/job/118102127308"
  "2026-10-19T15:24:53.044Z",codex-agent,"Follow-up to the recorded Windows list observation: all unchanged get/list/context latency jobs subsequently passed on Linux, macOS and Windows at native-context implementation head 63d359e. Exact p50/p95 values and unchanged ceilings are retained in docs/benchmarks/native-context-gates-2026-10-19.json and CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39273842181. No list implementation or latency threshold was changed for this follow-up. The earlier miss remains a bounded observed result, not proof of its cause."
  "2026-10-21T16:54:28.034Z",codex-agent,"Extend the existing performance item with a reproducible 1k/10k/50k synthetic no-git benchmark against pm-cli 2026.10.21: context, next, list-open, search, get, claim, comment and update. Branch starts at main because PR 101 is still open. Retain the locked release-check oracle until that parity PR merges. Measure wall p50/p95, GNU time peak RSS, output bytes and exact stdout/stderr/status comparisons. Main currently refuses context at 10k and larger; report this as unsupported rather than a successful speed measurement. Profile before optimizing, preserve append-only history and all write-safety boundaries, then verify 50 concurrent writers and unchanged full gates."
  "2026-10-21T17:09:05.364Z",codex-agent,Benchmark calibration found that the current oracle changes list completeness from complete on a cold validation to unchecked on a warm cache read. The harness now compares only measured warm runs after fixed warmups; it does not normalize that receipt. Native list also receives the same fixed read clock as context. Syscall profiling is enabled outside timing windows; perf hardware sampling is refused by the host kernel and no host setting was changed.
  "2026-10-21T17:20:48.437Z",codex-agent,"Baseline 1k syscall diagnostics confirm the mutation locator dominates metadata work: claim 8042 statx calls, comment and update 6026 each. The candidate skips live metadata for unrelated regular entries while retaining target, directory and symlink checks. Claim attribution still fully validates every document in the same order, but retains only IDs and parents instead of complete payloads. Added strict corruption/duplicate checks, moved-target coverage, work-count regressions and a 50-process barrier test that requires every write and marker to survive without Git. Benchmark fixtures now include SDK-generated valid create/comment history and oracle verification; timed oracle children import only the real CLI after clock pinning."
  "2026-10-21T17:31:42.918Z",codex-agent,"Draft PR 102 is open at f1abf67. Added an exact-head dedicated-runner benchmark to avoid the development host contention, and an automated behavioral revert proof that restores only full-corpus retention and per-entry metadata work, requires the specific two regression assertions to fail, then restores exact source bytes and requires both to pass. The full benchmark keeps all 20 measured launches per runtime/case and two warmups. Existing release thresholds remain unchanged. No merge or release is requested."
  "2026-10-21T17:42:57.845Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof passed at 124975a on a dedicated runner: reverted only full-payload lineage retention and unrelated-entry metadata scanning; each new regression failed its specific assertion (exit 101, zero passed and one failed). Exact source bytes were then restored and both regressions passed individually (exit 0, one passed each). The receipt source hashes match the package source. Local cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib also passed all 278 tests with zero failures or ignored tests. Receipt: docs/benchmarks/native-hot-path-revert-2026-10-21.json. Full 20-sample 1k/10k/50k benchmark and unchanged aggregate gates remain pending."
