  "2026-10-22T11:49:44.178Z",codex-agent,"Final receipt-head CI 39764251511 exposed a real event-order race in the interrupt fix, not a load timeout. Ordinary tests and macOS/Windows full gates passed, but Linux instrumented harness observed SIGTERM exit 1 instead of 143: the child termination callback can reject before the parent signal callback runs. Reopening this verification round before accepting the final head. Will route parent and child SIGINT/SIGTERM through shared cleanup, and add deterministic parent-only and child-only controls alongside process-group delivery. The earlier code-head Linux full pass remains historical evidence, not proof that this race is fixed. Also merged current origin/main tracker reconciliation before these changes."
  "2026-10-22T12:05:01.618Z",codex-agent,"Corrected interrupt behavior uses one cleanup function for both parent signals and cargo termination receipts, so either event order restores both exact source files and exits 130/143. Deterministic child-only controls reproduce the old callback race: both exit 1 before the fix. Final independent reverts: removing only child-signal dispatch fails cargo-only tests 2/2; removing only parent listeners fails parent-only restoration tests 2/2; each restored selection passes 2/2, with exact source-byte restoration after each control. Exact commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"cargo only\" scripts/harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"parent only\" scripts/harness.test.mts. The fixture now publishes its PID by rename and validates a positive ordinary PID before signalling; this fixes a test handoff hazard found during verification, without loosening restoration or exit assertions. Final full harness passes 19/19, zero failed/canceled/skipped; five bounded six-signal stress runs pass 30/30; the linked selection passes 6/6; strict no-emit erasable TypeScript checking passes. Fresh full CI is required for this correction; old failed receipt-head CI is not accepted as a pass."
  "2026-10-22T12:26:41.114Z",codex-agent,"Corrected code head 2cb5a578eb29d92e1602d268ded97a5bcb0601e6 passed the full Linux release gate including the instrumented harness that exposed the earlier race (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39775652585/job/119813788515). Ordinary and instrumented Rust runs each passed 582 tests across 22 suites, zero failed or ignored. Lines 14062/14062, functions 1472/1472, regions 23500/23500 and branches 3302/3302 are all exactly 100 percent with unchanged scope/thresholds. Audit, changelog and strict tracker health passed. The fresh real Rust revert-proof job also passed both intended assertion failures and both restored successes (https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39775652577/job/119813788472). The local full Node harness is 19/19; parent-only and cargo-only reverts each fail 2/2 and pass restored; signal stress is 30/30. The prior receipt-head assertion failure was corrected, not retried away or called a timeout. Releasing this verification claim with status retained in_progress; final receipt-head CI will be recorded in PR 102. No thread reply/resolution, PR merge or release."
  "2026-10-22T15:15:11.451Z",codex-agent,"New PR 102 review round: pulled remote head 0bcc6b3; origin/main is already an ancestor. Verified unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6vP3SE: paired native benchmark fingerprint refusal is incorrectly conditional on CI metadata, so a local identical baseline is accepted. Will remove only that condition, add a real non-git CLI regression with BENCH_BASE_SHA absent, prove it fails with the guard reverted, and inspect the whole PR for related self-comparison paths. Latest CodeRabbit review has no Outside diff range findings. Prior completed work and append-only histories remain intact."
